From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:51:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 200/204] security/tpm: Leave room for the payload in the TPM
 1.2 log

With TPM_LOG_TPM1 the measurement log in cbmem (CBMEM_ID_TCPA_TCG_LOG)
is also the log area that the ACPI TCPA table points to: acpi.c finds
the entry and publishes its size as LAML. The entry is sized for
coreboot's own 50 entries, about 4 KiB. A UEFI payload that logs into
the bootloader's TCPA table (SecurityPkg TcgDxe as a payload) appends
its events there, and those of the Secure Boot variables alone carry
the whole db and KEK: they do not fit, TcgDxe extends the PCR and drops
the event, and the log no longer replays to the PCRs.

Allocate the log with at least the 64 KiB that acpi.c gives the TCPA
log when it creates one itself.

TEST=QEMU q35 with swtpm as a TPM 1.2, TPM_MEASURED_BOOT and the
ouroBIOS payload: the TCPA log holds coreboot's CBFS measurements, then
the payload's events, and replays to the PCR values read back from the
TPM.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c b/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c
index 453e74b4e8..dc1f64eab6 100644
--- a/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c
+++ b/src/security/tpm/tspi/log-tpm1.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <symbols.h>
 #include <cbmem.h>
+#include <commonlib/bsd/helpers.h>
 #include <vb2_sha.h>
 
 void *tpm1_log_cbmem_init(void)
@@ -28,7 +29,13 @@ void *tpm1_log_cbmem_init(void)
 		if (tclt)
 			return tclt;
 
-		tpm_log_len = sizeof(*tclt) + MAX_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES * sizeof(tclt->entries[0]);
+		/*
+		 * This table is also the log area of the ACPI TCPA table, where
+		 * a UEFI payload logs its own events after coreboot's: leave
+		 * room for them, as much as acpi.c gives a log of its own.
+		 */
+		tpm_log_len = MAX(sizeof(*tclt) + MAX_TPM_LOG_ENTRIES * sizeof(tclt->entries[0]),
+				  64 * KiB);
 		tclt = cbmem_add(CBMEM_ID_TCPA_TCG_LOG, tpm_log_len);
 		if (!tclt)
 			return NULL;
